 "documents": {
  "attachments": [
   {
    "name": "ambulance_agreement.txt",
    "text": "Lifeline Event Medics\nBookings Office\n\nFebruary 9, 2027\n\nDear Priya Raman,\n\nThank you for your booking and payment. This letter is your agreement with us for ambulance cover at the Saltmarsh Community Run 7K on March 27, 2027. One ambulance and two paramedics will be on site at the top of Rope Walk, in place by 07:00, and will stay until the race has finished. Booking reference EV-36235.\n\nOur crew leader will find your race director when they arrive.\n\nKind regards,\nAnita Bose\nBookings Manager\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "crowd_plan.txt",
    "text": "Saltmarsh Community Run 7K - crowd notes\nSaturday 27 March 2027 / contact Priya Raman 555-0133\ntotal 750 incl 750 runners. Few people come just to watch.\n\nhired radio or 2 last time for start team, useful. short briefing for early arrivals. no complaints from runners\n\nVIEWING\n3 barriered areas: finish Market Square, turn at Abbey Road, start the top of Rope Walk. approx 1000 total @ 2 per sqm. over expected numbers\n\nSTART\nall start together 08:00 after warm-up + countdown. popular w/ runners\n\nSTEWARDS\n15 stewards (approx 1:50), 2 supervisors, rota by position, briefing 1hr before\n\nEXIT\nprizes then tea. people head off when ready. buses nearby\n\nCONTROL\nPriya Raman at control w/ radio to all supervisors. can hold wave, stop race, use PA. sups call in if area getting full\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "insurance.txt",
    "text": "CERTIFICATE OF LIABILITY INSURANCE\nCertificate no. PH-97916\nIssued: January 7, 2026\n\nINSURER: Meridian Mutual Insurance\nPOLICY NUMBER: GL-873033\n\nNAMED INSURED: Saltmarsh Running Group\nDESCRIPTION OF OPERATIONS: Public liability for a foot race, the Saltmarsh Community Run 7K\nVENUE: Eastfield, Port Halden\n\nPOLICY PERIOD\nEffective: January 1, 2026\nExpiry: December 31, 2026\n\nLIMIT OF LIABILITY: $5,000,000 each occurrence\n\nThis certificate is issued for information only and confers no rights upon the holder beyond those of the policy.\n\nCertificate holder: City of Port Halden, Events Office\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "medical_plan.txt",
    "text": "Saltmarsh Community Run 7K - medical notes\nSaturday 27 March 2027 / gun 08:00 / 750 runners / 7K\ncontact Priya Raman 555-0133\nOn-site ambulance cover is set out in the attached paperwork from Lifeline Event Medics.\n\nbg: committee done this race yrs. one long time member is retired paramedic but runs race herself, not on duty\n\nFIRST AID\n3 posts (start, finish, midpoint). 6 qualified first aiders. nowhere more than 1.5km from a post. 2 bike responders w/ defibs\n\nWEATHER / WATER\nwater every 2.5k. forecast check -48h and -2h. >28C earlier start or shorter course. >32C cancel. foil + warm tent at finish if cold/wet\n\nHOSPITAL\nPort Halden General Hospital, 7km from finish. pickup point the top of Rope Walk, route walked w/ first aiders. ED told date + numbers\n\nCOMMS\nradios on medical channel at all posts + bikes, phones backup. amb calls go via medical lead, who gives crew the barrier to come to\n\nLEAD\nGrace Lindqvist, registered paramedic, on site from -1hr til last runner in. can withdraw any runner\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "police_letter.txt",
    "text": "PORT HALDEN POLICE SERVICE\nTraffic and Events Division\n200 Prince Street, Port Halden\n\n9 February 2027\n\nPriya Raman\nSaltmarsh Running Group\n\nRe: Saltmarsh Community Run 7K, 27 March 2027\n\nDear Priya Raman,\n\nI confirm that this Division will provide a police escort for the above event on 27 March 2027. Two motorcycle officers will accompany the lead runner along the route through Eastfield, and one traffic unit will be stationed at Rope Walk from 07:00 until the last runner has cleared the course.\n\nPlease send your final course map to this office no later than seven days before the event.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nSgt. Karen Holt\nTraffic and Events Division\nReference EV-98574\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "race_plan.txt",
    "text": "Saltmarsh Community Run 7K: how the race will work\n\nPrepared by Priya Raman (Race Director), Saltmarsh Running Group. Last updated 9 February 2027.\n\nThis is our plan for race day, Saturday 27 March 2027. We expect 750 runners over 7K (7 km). Numbers can be collected from the top of Rope Walk from an hour before we go at 08:00, and we aim to have the last finisher home by 09:30.\n\nThe route takes in Rope Walk, Eastern Link Road, Abbey Road and Canon Road, and the City would need to close all of these for us. On the way round we cross High Street, Tram Street, Victoria Road and Ferry Road. We finish in Market Square.\n\nIt's a lovely route through the old part of town, though there isn't much room. We measured Rope Walk at 3.5 metres and Canon Road at 5 metres, doorstep to doorstep. Two cars can't pass on Abbey Road. People watching tend to stand in doorways.\n\nOur club has put on races for some years now and we keep to the same simple format: chip timing, water on the course, and a hot drink at the end. Results go up on our website the same evening.\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "traffic_plan.txt",
    "text": "TRAFFIC MANAGEMENT PLAN\nEvent: Saltmarsh Community Run 7K\nDate: Saturday 27 March 2027\nApplicant: Saltmarsh Running Group\nPrepared by: Corvus Temporary Works\nIssue: 3.1\n\n1. Scope\nThis plan describes how traffic will be managed for the Saltmarsh Community Run 7K, a 7K race in the Eastfield area of Port Halden with a 08:00 start. It has been prepared to accompany the permit application and should be read with the race plan. Police attendance is covered in the attached correspondence.\n\n2. Road closures\nTemporary closures will be in force as follows, with barriers and advance signing supplied by Northline Barriers.\n- Rope Walk, Chapel Row to Mill Road: closed 07:00 to 10:00\n- Eastern Link Road, Mill Road to Weir Street: closed 07:00 to 10:00\n- Abbey Road, Salter Way to Chapel Row: closed 07:00 to 10:00\n- Canon Road, Copper Row to Salter Way: closed 07:00 to 10:00\n\n3. Major crossings\nEach major crossing has its own control point, staffed from 07:00 until the last runner has passed.\n- High Street at Eastern Link Road: 4 traffic marshals with stop/go boards, one supervisor\n- Tram Street at Rope Walk: 4 traffic marshals with stop/go boards, one supervisor\n- Victoria Road at Abbey Road: 4 traffic marshals with stop/go boards, one supervisor\n- Ferry Road at Canon Road: 2 traffic marshals with stop/go boards, one supervisor\n\n4. Diversions\nSigned diversions will operate for the duration of the closures.\n- Rope Walk: traffic diverted via Queen's Road and Church Road, signed from Mill Road\n- Eastern Link Road: traffic diverted via Prince Street and Church Road, signed from Salter Way\n- Abbey Road: traffic diverted via Station Road and Canal Road, signed from Chapel Row\n- Canon Road: traffic diverted via Dock Road and Church Road, signed from Vine Street\n\n5. Emergency vehicle access\nA clear lane of at least 3.5 m will be kept along the closed section for emergency vehicles. Barrier staff hold radios on the event channel and can open any closure within two minutes on request from the event controller, who is in direct contact with the police and ambulance control rooms.\n\n6. Notification\nAll frontages on the closed streets receive a letter drop 21 days before the event, with a further reminder at 7 days. Advance notice signs go up 10 days before, and bus operators have been given the closure times.\n\n7. Reopening\nRoads will be reopened following the conclusion of the event, once barriers and equipment have been removed by the contractor.\n\nThe route has changed little from last time. Where it has changed, we have tried to keep a clear run for the field, and we welcome any comments from the Events Office on how signed diversions are usually handled in the city.\n"
   }
  ],
  "cover_letter": "Hello,\n\nI am writing on behalf of our organisation about this year's race.\n\nHere is our application for the Saltmarsh Community Run 7K, Saturday 27 March 2027. 750 runners, 7K, off at 08:00, around Eastfield. I've attached ambulance_agreement.txt, crowd_plan.txt, insurance.txt, medical_plan.txt, police_letter.txt, race_plan.txt, traffic_plan.txt.\n\nWe look forward to hearing from you.\n\nThanks,\nPriya\n\nPriya Raman, Saltmarsh Running Group\n555-0133\n",
